# Test: ExpansionGuard RAII cleanup on macro expansion error (MH0 regression test)
# Without the ExpansionGuard fix, a macro expansion error would leak depth/blackhole
# state, causing the next call to the same macro to spuriously fail with
# "recursive macro expansion detected".
# This test verifies that after an expansion-time error (syntax class mismatch),
# a subsequent valid call to the SAME macro succeeds.

[macro wraps-let [let binding@LetDecl]
  [quote 42]]

# First call: invalid argument (plain integer) → macro-expansion-error
[wraps-let 99]

---
# Second call: valid [let ...] argument → should succeed
# Without ExpansionGuard, this would spuriously error with "recursive macro expansion"
[wraps-let [let x 1]]
=== error
macro expansion error: macro 'wraps-let': argument 'binding' expected LetDecl, got Literal (defined at 11:1-11:15)
